{"name":"Potato Chip","hex":"#fddc57","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"potato chip","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of a batch of pieces of potato cut into elongated cubes and fried; a chip or chipped potato, usually larger than American French fries.","A potato crisp, a thin slice of potato that has been fried."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/potato_chip"}],"entries":[{"title":"Potato chips","blocks":[{"text":"Potato chips or crisps are thin slices of potato that have been deep-fried, baked, or air-fried until crunchy. They are commonly served as a snack, appetizer or side dish. Basic potato chips are cooked and salted; additional varieties are manufactured using various seasonings, flavorings and ingredients including herbs, spices, cheeses, other natural flavors, artificial flavors, and additives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Potato-Chips.jpg/330px-Potato-Chips.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potato_chips"},{"title":"Potato","blocks":[{"text":"The potato is a starchy tuberous vegetable native to the Americas that is consumed as a staple food in many parts of the world. Potatoes are underground stem tubers of the plant Solanum tuberosum, a perennial in the nightshade family Solanaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Patates.jpg/330px-Patates.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potato"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Production_of_homemade_chips_%284%29.JPG/500px-Production_of_homemade_chips_%284%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Production_of_homemade_chips_%284%29.JPG/1280px-Production_of_homemade_chips_%284%29.JPG?utm_source=en.